hello and thank you for joining us today  my name is dr. Ruth Whittaker director  of the laboratory Quality Assurance and  proficiency program at RTI International  RTI International and its Centre for  forensic sciences helps bridge the gap  between science and law as we support  forensic science laboratories and  practitioners while promoting innovation  and advancement solving the most  challenging issues in forensic science  lab roots is pleased to assemble  academic scientists research scholars  biochemists toxicology and healthcare  professionals and top leaders for both  industry and academia from all over the  world to its inaugural forensics and  toxicology conference forensics and  toxicology 2019 shares a deep insight  into the evolving research and trends  and cutting-edge technology applications  in forensic toxicology pharmaceutical  and environmental toxicology and  forensic science disciplines the agenda  not only aims to deliver a educational  opportunity for attendees but to promote  top-level research thus making the  discussions and presentations focused on  recent outstanding achievements in this  pioneering field this day will be  dedicated to cover a wide spectrum of  themes and will tackle important issues  including human health impacts of  environmental chemical exposures new  concepts in forensic investigation  generating authentic research experience  in forensic based projects in vitro  screening approaches to estimate human a  patek responses to xenobiotic exposures  and what's new in forensic toxicology  and pharmacology as it relates to drugs  and standards composed of five  thought-provoking discussions by  nationally recognized experts the  program kicks off with a keynote  delivery by dr. Linda Birnbaum director  of the National Institute of  Environmental Health Sciences and  board-certified toxicologist addressing  chemical exposures and how they need in  packed  health and identify opportunities to  change our environment and in the  closing keynote dr. Henry Lee one of the  world's foremost forensic scientists  will explain the interaction between  crime scene and forensic science and  different types of evidence and  techniques used in the forensic field  and more this conference will deliberate  and desist and discuss all different  aspects of this topic and provide a  dynamic interactive platform to maximize  learning via live streaming video  webcasts and networking with peers in  the virtual lounge be sure to enter the  exhibit hall and explore showcased  technologies at the booths and engage  real-time with sponsor representatives  for a multi-faceted perspective on the  latest innovations and novel  applications in forensic and laboratory  medicine and medical technology on  behalf of the invited presenters and  sponsors lab roots is proud to bring you  this online symposium and collaborative  informative experience we're looking  forward to enlightening sessions from  distinguished speakers sharing new and  exciting insights in facilitating  scientific advancements and future  collaborations in forensics and  toxicology thank you for your  participation and enjoy
 

